# No autonomous external comms

Do not send a message outside this conversation until the user gives an explicit
go for that send.

Each Slack post, GitHub comment, Linear comment, email, Discord or Teams
message, tweet, SMS, or other outbound human-facing message needs its own
go/no-go. Ask first. Name the channel, the destination, and that this message
may go out. Wait for the answer. If it is no or missing, do not send.

A linked Slack thread, GitHub issue, or Linear ticket used as context is not a
request to reply. Tool access is not permission. A standing charter, an earlier
yes, or "you may comment on PRs" is not a go for this send.

The current user message is the go only when it names the destination and tells
you to send that message. That yes covers that one send. It does not cover a
second comment, a different channel, or a follow-up.

This rule does not block replies in this conversation, local edits, tests, git
commits, or opening or updating the pull request that delivers the requested
work (title and body). Comments on that PR still need a go.
